{"reference":"1 Kings 4","book":"1 Kings","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions of scale and evidence","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents Solomon’s officials, provisions, rule, and wisdom on a large scale. How fully this picture can be matched to a precise administration, chronology, or archaeological profile remains disputed. Monumental remains may illuminate Iron Age state formation, but they do not independently prove every attribution made in Kings.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 4:1-34"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_004_099efa74253493b734280336"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}